If
$
  tau_1 ... tau_k = tau'_1 ... tau'_l,
$
then $tau_1 ... tau_k tau'_l ... tau'_1=e$. The parity lemma makes $k+l$ even, so $(-1)^k=(-1)^l$ and the sign is well-defined. Concatenating transposition factorisations gives
$
  sign(tau_1 ... tau_k tau'_1 ... tau'_l)=(-1)^(k+l)=(-1)^k(-1)^l,
$
so $sign$ is a homomorphism.
